    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0411" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg361"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Fava to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of His Majesty the King of Italy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                22, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to the note of
                    the honorable Department of State, bearing date of November 18, 1890, I have the
                    honor herewith to transmit to your excellency, together with certain
                    observations, (1) the draft of an agreement supplementary to the convention of
                    extradition which is now in force between Italy and the United States; (2) a
                    draft of a naturalization convention between our two countries, on the model of
                    that between the United States and Belgium, as suggested by the Federal
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The propriety and desirability which have already been recognized by our two
                    Governments to conclude these two arrangements with as little delay as possible
                    do not leave any doubt in my mind with regard to their acceptance by the U. S.
                    Government, which acceptance would be very gratifying to the Government of His
                    Majesty.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fava.</hi></signed></closer>




